# Workflow engine rules

## Primary rule
The workflow engine is the single source of truth for path decisions.
The UI renders engine outputs. The AI layer assists — it does not decide.

## Engine responsibilities
- classify enquiry type
- determine next required question
- evaluate decision points
- surface support options
- trigger escalation flags
- enforce stop conditions
- emit trace objects

## What the engine must NOT do
- call the AI layer to make path decisions
- guess at facts not yet captured

## What the AI layer must NOT do
- decide legal entitlement
- invent local authority rules
- override escalation logic
- fabricate facts not in session state
- return freeform text that bypasses schema validation

## Rule traceability
Every significant decision must include:
- rule_code that fired
- trigger_facts that caused it
- workflow_version_id active at evaluation time
